## Control {{controlId}}: Limit Unsuccessful Logon Attempts

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization limits unsuccessful logon attempts within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Account lockout enforcement is implemented through Azure AD Smart Lockout, Conditional Access sign-in frequency policies, and risk-based authentication that automatically responds to brute-force and credential-stuffing attacks.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
Azure AD Smart Lockout automatically locks accounts after repeated failed authentication attempts. Conditional Access policies across {{caPoliciesTotalCount}} configurations enforce sign-in frequency controls and risk-based responses. High-risk sign-in attempts are blocked or require additional authentication factors before proceeding.
{{else}}
Conditional Access sign-in frequency policies have not been configured. Unsuccessful logon limits rely on Azure AD Smart Lockout default settings, pending enhanced policy configuration.
{{/if}}

{{#if policies}}
The following Conditional Access policies enforce logon attempt restrictions:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Enforces {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}} with session controls for failed attempt thresholds.
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

{{#if signInLogsAvailable}}
Sign-in logs capture {{signInLogsCount}} authentication events, including failed attempts, for audit and incident investigation. Security alerts are generated for anomalous lockout patterns.
{{/if}}

{{#if infraResources}}
Supporting infrastructure:
{{#each infraResources}}
- {{resourceType}} "{{name}}"{{#if properties.retention_days}} (retention: {{properties.retention_days}} days){{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

